## Recommended Workflow for Future Graphs

Based on the investigation, here is the most reliable way to generate or update your graphs:

### 1. Configuration ([config.yml](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/config.yml))
Always use a [config.yml](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/config.yml) file in your project root with the following mandatory structure:

```yaml
select_origin: directory
files_origin: "Empresas" # Directory containing your .md files
export_target: "."       # Where to save the output
title: "Project Name"
history: false
lang: en # Only 'en' or 'fr' are supported in v2.6.0
record_types:
  undefined:
    fill: "#858585"
    stroke: "#858585"
link_types:
  undefined:
    stroke: simple
    color: "#e1e1e1"
```

### 2. Execution
Run the following command in your terminal from the project root:

```powershell
npx cosma modelize
```

This command will read your Markdown files, process wiki-links (`[[target]]`), and generate a new [cosmoscope.html](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosmoscope.html) (which you can rename as needed).

